==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{m|frm|bidon||small portable container, sealed and made of wood or metal}}, from {{etyl|non|fr}} *{{m|non||bida, *biða|container, vessel}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fr}} {{m|gem-pro|*bidōn}}, {{m|gem-pro|*bidjan||tub, vessel, vat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fr}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰidʰ-||pot, bucket, barrel}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-||to weave, bind}}. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|biða||milkbucket}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{m|no|bide||churn}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{m|no|bidne||vessel}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|fidēlia||clay or glass vessel}}, {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|πίθος||wine barrel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-bidon.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/bi.dɔ̃/|lang=fr}}
* {{rhymes|dɔ̃|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# [[can]], [[tin]], [[canister]]
